swer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186695535} :answer-field/id #uuid "c30e025d-c286-5242-a61d-30d613984a92" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186695556}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3efede5c-192f-5448-a02d-2de13944b43f" :question/problem "Calculate $AB$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nComplete the product $AB$ below. Rows and columns are shown in matrix order.\n\n| | Column 1 | Column 2 | Column 3 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Row 1 | {{field-1}} | $2$ | {{field-2}} |\n| Row 2 | $-5$ | {{field-3}} | $-3$ |\n| Row 3 | {{field-4}} | $1$ | {{field-5}} |\n" :question/worked-solution "Multiply each row of $A$ by each column of $B$, adding the three pairwise products. The supplied entries and the missing entries all follow this rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{11} &= 2\\cdot1+(-1)\\cdot(-2)+1\\cdot3 = 7 \\\\ c_{12} &= 2\\cdot2+(-1)\\cdot1+1\\cdot(-1) = 2 \\\\ c_{13} &= 2\\cdot(-1)+(-1)\\cdot2+1\\cdot1 = -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{21} &= 1\\cdot1+0\\cdot(-2)+(-2)\\cdot3 = -5 \\\\ c_{22} &= 1\\cdot2+0\\cdot1+(-2)\\cdot(-1) = 4 \\\\ c_{23} &= 1\\cdot(-1)+0\\cdot2+(-2)\\cdot1 = -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{31} &= 0\\cdot1+2\\cdot(-2)+1\\cdot3 = -1 \\\\ c_{32} &= 0\\cdot2+2\\cdot1+1\\cdot(-1) = 1 \\\\ c_{33} &= 0\\cdot(-1)+2\\cdot2+1\\cdot1 = 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\nTherefore,\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186695558 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6594f5e0-32cb-5f94-b2fd-10098b5e7a5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186695537}] :answer-field/correct {:ans