n\nand\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nComplete the product $AB$ below. Rows and columns are shown in matrix order.\n\n| | Column 1 | Column 2 | Column 3 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Row 1 | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |\n| Row 2 | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |\n| Row 3 | {{field-7}} | {{field-8}} | {{field-9}} |\n" :question/worked-solution "Multiply each row of $A$ by each column of $B$, adding the three pairwise products. Compute all nine entries in row order.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{11} &= 1\\cdot2+(-2)\\cdot1+3\\cdot(-1) = -3 \\\\ c_{12} &= 1\\cdot(-1)+(-2)\\cdot3+3\\cdot2 = -1 \\\\ c_{13} &= 1\\cdot1+(-2)\\cdot(-2)+3\\cdot3 = 14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{21} &= (-1)\\cdot2+2\\cdot1+1\\cdot(-1) = -1 \\\\ c_{22} &= (-1)\\cdot(-1)+2\\cdot3+1\\cdot2 = 9 \\\\ c_{23} &= (-1)\\cdot1+2\\cdot(-2)+1\\cdot3 = -2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{31} &= 2\\cdot2+1\\cdot1+(-2)\\cdot(-1) = 7 \\\\ c_{32} &= 2\\cdot(-1)+1\\cdot3+(-2)\\cdot2 = -3 \\\\ c_{33} &= 2\\cdot1+1\\cdot(-2)+(-2)\\cdot3 = -6\\end{aligned}\n$$\nTherefore,\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -1 & 14 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 \\\\ 7 & -3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186695737 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82fcad6c-456e-577d-8c68-84742806402b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186695749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82fcad6c-456e-577d-8c68-84742806402b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186695749} :answer-field/id #uuid "26ed4875-6c38-5f0d-b6b9-7a1c5e92d1c1" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186695727} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00747b22-888b-5abd-b68c-85b8c5625432" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186695716}